  "verbalization": "Isosorbide Mononitrate, a nitrate, is linked to Gucy1a3 through a series of biological pathways that involve vasodilation and the binding of nitroglycerin-like compounds. The evidence suggests that Isosorbide Mononitrate, as part of the nitrate class, interacts with Gucy1a3 via a mechanism involving vasodilating agents. This is supported by the shared lowest common ancestors in multiple paths, which indicate a hierarchical relationship between nitrates and vasodilating agents. The presence of Gucy1a3 as a target in both nitrate and nitroglycerin pathways highlights a potential role in the physiological effects of nitrates, such as relaxing blood vessels. The integration of these pathways underscores a general mechanism by which nitrates, through their interaction with Gucy1a3, contribute to vasodilation, suggesting a broader functional role in cardiovascular regulation.",
